WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:06.994
Swallow spent the next day giving away more gold.

2
00:00:06.995 --> 00:00:10.957
He gave gold to farmers whose crops had failed.

3
00:00:10.958 --> 00:00:15.749
He gave some to a woman who fed stray cats.

4
00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:20.457
"I need to rest for a little while," he thought.

5
00:00:20.458 --> 00:00:28.041
He landed on a tree. Below, two men were talking.

6
00:00:28.042 --> 00:00:36.082
"Yes," one said. "A swallow dropped a piece of gold right at my feet."

7
00:00:36.083 --> 00:00:40.624
"It happened to me too," his friend said.

8
00:00:40.625 --> 00:00:46.916
A woman walked by. "Are you talking about the bird with the gold?"

9
00:00:46.917 --> 00:00:50.080
When they nodded, she smiled.

10
00:00:50.081 --> 00:00:59.374
"The swallow visited me too. I bought food, candles, and wood for the fireplace."

11
00:00:59.375 --> 00:01:04.155
More people gathered, sharing stories about the bird.

12
00:01:04.156 --> 00:01:12.916
Then one man frowned. "That bird ruined our statue!"

13
00:01:12.917 --> 00:01:17.014
"It's just a statue," someone said.

14
00:01:17.015 --> 00:01:24.374
"Which is more important? A beautiful statue or the people of this town?"

15
00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:28.618
The man grumbled again. But then he shrugged.

16
00:01:28.619 --> 00:01:36.291
"I suppose you're right. It's better for people to have food and shelter."

17
00:01:36.292 --> 00:01:44.082
Swallow flew off to tell the statue what he heard.

18
00:01:44.083 --> 00:01:48.291
"People are very grateful!" Swallow said.

19
00:01:48.292 --> 00:01:53.749
"I don't know how to thank you," the statue said.

20
00:01:53.750 --> 00:02:01.390
"You don't have to," Swallow said. "Helping people brings me joy.

21
00:02:01.391 --> 00:02:04.749
And I've learned something new about beauty.

22
00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:11.494
But Prince, you have one last piece of gold.

23
00:02:11.495 --> 00:02:13.434
Do you want to keep it?"

24
00:02:13.435 --> 00:02:18.916
"No," the statue said. "I have a plan.

25
00:02:18.917 --> 00:02:22.791
Can you help me once more before you leave?"

26
00:02:22.792 --> 00:02:28.416
"Of course! I'll do it in the morning."

27
00:02:28.417 --> 00:02:33.124
That evening the two friends looked out over the town.

28
00:02:33.125 --> 00:02:37.666
"Does the town look different?" Swallow asked.

29
00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:40.934
"It's brighter," the statue said.

30
00:02:40.935 --> 00:02:44.874
"Candles glow in windows.

31
00:02:44.875 --> 00:02:49.083
Fires burn in hearths, and listen!

32
00:02:49.084 --> 00:02:53.957
People are talking and laughing."

33
00:02:53.958 --> 00:03:00.892
"It's a wonderful sound."

34
00:03:00.893 --> 00:03:06.832
At sunrise the statue told Swallow who should get the last gold piece.

35
00:03:06.833 --> 00:03:11.624
"Why him?" Swallow asked in surprise.

36
00:03:11.625 --> 00:03:19.108
"You'll see," the statue said.

37
00:03:19.109 --> 00:03:22.147
Swallow flew to a cottage.

38
00:03:22.148 --> 00:03:27.957
Outside he saw firewood, a cow, and chickens.

39
00:03:27.958 --> 00:03:32.582
Inside, a young man sat writing.

40
00:03:32.583 --> 00:03:38.625
Suddenly he sighed and lay down his pen.

41
00:03:38.626 --> 00:03:48.562
"Why do I waste my time? No one will ever read my stories."

42
00:03:48.563 --> 00:03:51.288
"Oh!" Swallow thought.

43
00:03:51.289 --> 00:03:55.374
"This young man has plenty of food.

44
00:03:55.375 --> 00:03:58.624
But he needs something else."

45
00:03:58.625 --> 00:04:04.082
Whoosh! Swallow swooped in and dropped the gold.

46
00:04:04.083 --> 00:04:11.340
The writer cheered. "What a gift!

47
00:04:11.341 --> 00:04:19.582
Now I can publish my stories." He stared at the gold.

48
00:04:19.583 --> 00:04:27.083
"And maybe I have an idea for a new one."
